{"chapter-slug":"rw6-50 I","paragraph":466,"wording":"[Autumn Knight]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Another book. This one—Necromancy, Its Rise and Fall, by Sir Hilten, [Autumn Knight] of the Order of Seasons. She hadn’t read it. Ilvriss went on.","id":"0aed5ea9-00ac-58af-92df-bf0f491e8cd0"}
{"chapter-slug":"rw6-42 E","paragraph":448,"wording":"[Autumn Knight]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Sir Kelm was a Knight of the Autumn, or a Fall Knight. Or an [Autumn Knight] if you wanted to be precise, but ‘Fall Knight’ was a joke the younger members of the Order sometimes used to refer to the lower level of skill in combat the Knights of the Autumn possessed. They were scholars or [Knights] who pursued projects or simply took to magic more than most [Knights].","id":"ded7ae79-5cbb-51af-832f-396ddab76fde"}
